{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell","id":1179503,"title":"Trinity Developers on 16Miles2Hell","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-26T06:25:56-08:00","id":1179503,"title":"Trinity Developers on 16Miles2Hell","content":"This week, Phlip and I had the extreme joy of hosting Ian Watson, Danielle Lauzon, and Eddy Webb on the podcast to talk about Trinity, the upcoming Kickstarter, and sci-fi gaming in general. Though we'd love for you to listen to the whole podcast, the interview starts at 25:15 for people that just want to jump right in! <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">We're not done talking sci-fi yet, mofos! After last week's explosive chat about all things Star Wars, Rick and Philip are back to bring the deets on the best Science Fiction Table Top game ever - AEON! As the Trinity Contiumm and Trinity Contriuum: Aeon Kickstarter go live next week, we have invited the Trinity Head Pooh-bah Ian Watson, the Storypath Guru Daniella Lauzon, and That Guy Over There Eddy Webb to the Action Mega Bunker to talk all things Trinity. Excitement! Danger! Romance? </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Will</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Onyx Path Publishing</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">save the world for ALL MANKIND? All of these things and more this week on 16Miles2Hell!&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://16miles2hell.com/16miles2hell-24\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://16miles2hell.com/16miles2hell-24\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://16miles2hell.com/16miles2hell-24\" target=\"_blank\"> http://16miles2hell.com/16miles2hell-24 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Rick A. Carroll - Onyx Path Freelancer</b><br /> <b>Worked On</b>: Night Horrors: Enemy Action, Night Horrors: The Tormented<br /> <b>Working On: </b>Nada at the moment. Hire me!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2737-thrazghul","name":"Thrazghul","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T13:05:32-08:00","id":1179585,"title":"","content":"Huh. Trinity Battleground gets a bit of love in this. Awesome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T15:22:06-08:00","id":1179637,"title":"","content":"I will always give Battleground love. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Rick A. Carroll - Onyx Path Freelancer</b><br /> <b>Worked On</b>: Night Horrors: Enemy Action, Night Horrors: The Tormented<br /> <b>Working On: </b>Nada at the moment. Hire me!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2737-thrazghul","name":"Thrazghul","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T06:53:23-08:00","id":1179814,"title":"","content":"I bought Battleground to complete my collection but have never played it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T09:06:48-08:00","id":1179845,"title":"","content":"Can someone post a summary of the interview? I have some difficulty with the nuances of spoken English.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","name":"Starkiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T06:21:30-08:00","id":1180404,"title":"","content":"I'm still listening, but some points so far:<br /> <br /> - Core book is modern day, action-adventure kinda like the the Bourne Identity, etc.<br /> - Aeon book will be the old Trinity setting<br /> - Both these books will be in the kickstarter<br /> - There was a joke? about including Trinity Battlegrounds in the Kickstarter. Someone at OP is a big fan of Battlegrounds, so if they can make it work, they would like to put out a minis game<br /> - The Trinity background has some minor changes - The Legions aren't independent military contractors any more. Too many bad associations with Blackwater, etc. They're now a military arm of the UN.<br /> - The Orders and Proxies haven't changed.<br /> - The game should be recognizable as Trinity<br /> - Some minor changes to how the Esperanza happened.<br /> - The game has a concept of multiple timelines. If you want to play the old timeline, with the new rules, that's completely legit and supported.<br /> <br /> That's where I got to for now. I'll post more when I listen to more. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T08:52:09-08:00","id":1180430,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","name":"Starkiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T13:41:24-08:00","id":1180492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180404#post1180404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still listening, but some points so far:<br /> - The Trinity background has some minor changes - The Legions aren't independent military contractors any more. Too many bad associations with Blackwater, etc. They're now a military arm of the UN.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I hadn't heard that. I kinda thought PMCs would make the game the have a little more of a this-is-sic-fi-but-we're-really-talking-about-right-now kind of vibe. Could be pretty neato if they're mostly co-opted by the UN in that case too - private (para)military with UN oversight but oodles of gray area in terms of responsibility and oversight. I guess the UN having their own command and control armed forces does give a nice new world order feel though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T14:20:16-08:00","id":1180502,"title":"","content":"I'm not 100% sure, but I read somewhere that one of the developers said that some of the changes done to the aeon setting were done in order to create a more idealistic future, especially when it comes to the legions. I think it was done so players could feel more like heroes instead of ruthless mercenaries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T16:23:35-08:00","id":1180530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queen Anne Country</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180492#post1180492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. I hadn't heard that. I kinda thought PMCs would make the game the have a little more of a this-is-sic-fi-but-we're-really-talking-about-right-now kind of vibe. Could be pretty neato if they're mostly co-opted by the UN in that case too - private (para)military with UN oversight but oodles of gray area in terms of responsibility and oversight. I guess the UN having their own command and control armed forces does give a nice new world order feel though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Larssen will be putting up with crap from anyone, including the UN. I guess we'll see what she had to give up to get the veneer of respectability. I wonder what's going to happen to the Second Legion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T16:28:35-08:00","id":1180534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180404#post1180404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- There was a joke? about including Trinity Battlegrounds in the Kickstarter. Someone at OP is a big fan of Battlegrounds, so if they can make it work, they would like to put out a minis game</div> </div> </div> </div>From my listening, I think this is a bit of an over stretch. Mike Chaney loves Battleground and (jokingly?) frequently pitches for its return, but I didn\u2019t get the sense OPP is seriously thinking along that line at all.<br /> <br /> If others interpreted that differently, that\u2019s interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T16:34:31-08:00","id":1180537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180502#post1180502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not 100% sure, but I read somewhere that one of the developers said that some of the changes done to the aeon setting were done in order to create a more idealistic future, especially when it comes to the legions. I think it was done so players could feel more like heroes instead of ruthless mercenaries.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Trinity Continuum (including the AEon setting) is a hopeful, heroic place. Characters are striving for the future of humanity. Everything there is still recognisable from 1st ed, and everything you love is still there*, but 2nd ed has been written without the \u2018everyone secretly wants to screw everyone else over has torturous, murderous agendas\u2019 that (old) White Wolf seemed to (inadvertent) put into every setting back then.<br /> <br /> I was a huge fan of 1st ed, and I love what\u2019s gone into 2nd ed. I think/hope you will too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *Unless you love everyone murdering and screwing everyone else over <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":".  Stupid autocorrect 01-29-2018, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T16:40:42-08:00","id":1180541,"title":"","content":"- The Upeo Wa Macho will be playable right from the start<br /> - There will be a full Quantakinesis writeup in the Aeon book for any stories you might need it for<br /> - The PC's will have a &quot;skill&quot; for each Aptitude in their Mode and a Psi score and a Psi pool to use to power abilities<br /> - Ian has a document with 3 dozen ideas for expansion books. It's up to Rich to determine what, if any get made. It's possible to do a one-off for a book for a setting without having to support that book as a whole line. Examples - 1960's cop procedurals, or the XWF<br /> - The game is written and shouldn't have the same delays as Scion had<br /> - There are 3 developers for Trinity Continuum and Aeon (Ian, Danielle and John Snead)<br /> <br /> The End","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","user":"Spaaace","date":".  Noting that this is the end of the podcast 01-29-2018, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T16:48:25-08:00","id":1180544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180534#post1180534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From my listening, I think this is a bit of an over stretch. Mike Chaney loves Battleground and (jokingly?) frequently pitches for its return, but I didn\u2019t get the sense OPP is seriously thinking along that line at all.<br /> <br /> If others interpreted that differently, that\u2019s interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The line from the podcast that stood out for me is from Ian: &quot;There is support for it among the Onyx Path crew, so if we find a reasonable way to make it happen, it's probably going to happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think that's a pretty huge 'if', given that OP is a paper publishing company, not a minis company. Corvus Belli branched Infinity out from an in-house RPG to a mini wargame, so it's possible, but I wouldn't hold my breath. <br /> <br /> Personally, I would love to be able to pick up a PDF of the Battlegrounds rulebook as a stretch goal or add on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T17:07:53-08:00","id":1180547,"title":"","content":"Cool. I\u2019ll remain optimistic, and look for more things I can write for TC. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Everyone go back the Kickstarter when it opens. There are some stretch goals I want to be allowed to write!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T17:21:05-08:00","id":1180549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180541#post1180541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The PC's will have a &quot;skill&quot; for each Aptitude in their Mode and a Psi score and a Psi pool to use to power abilities</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of. Characters don\u2019t have to take a separate skill in each Mode (which is how I\u2019m reading what you\u2019ve said - apologies if I\u2019m incorrect) - Psi power activation is always Psi dots + Mode dots. If you have Psi 3 and Iatrosis 3, you roll 6 dice. <br /> <br /> I eliminated the 1st edition need for characters to base psi activation rolls on non-psi skills. Firstly, it meant characters had to spread their precious xp too thin, secondly, it meant you had to remember what level of Mode paired with what what skill, which slowed down play, and third, it made no sense that a vitakinetic needed training and experience in Medicine to be able to use psi, while a psychokinetic didn\u2019t need a PhD in aerodynamics to be able to fly.<br /> <br /> Once the campaign kicks off and the psi rules get offered for backers, I\u2019m happy to talk more about the design philosophies that went into it. Just make a thread and let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T17:49:50-08:00","id":1180551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180549#post1180549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kind of. Characters don\u2019t have to take a separate skill in each Mode (which is how I\u2019m reading what you\u2019ve said - apologies if I\u2019m incorrect) - Psi power activation is always Psi dots + Mode dots. If you have Psi 3 and Iatrosis 3, you roll 6 dice.<br /> <br /> I eliminated the 1st edition need for characters to base psi activation rolls on non-psi skills. Firstly, it meant characters had to spread their precious xp too thin, secondly, it meant you had to remember what level of Mode paired with what what skill, which slowed down play, and third, it made no sense that a vitakinetic needed training and experience in Medicine to be able to use psi, while a psychokinetic didn\u2019t need a PhD in aerodynamics to be able to fly.<br /> <br /> Once the campaign kicks off and the psi rules get offered for backers, I\u2019m happy to talk more about the design philosophies that went into it. Just make a thread and let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I reversed my mode and aptitude terms by mistake. I believe we're on the same page now. There's a rating (similar to a skill rating) for each mode in an aptitude. Ie. you could be a Vitakinetic with Iatrosis:3, Mentatis:1 and Algesis: 0 is how I understood it.<br /> <br /> I would love to know more when you can say more!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T18:07:55-08:00","id":1180558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/foru