le":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180558#post1180558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct, although those vitakinesis Modes aren\u2019t necessarily correct any more...</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that's just mean... \ud83d\ude1c","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T18:16:28-08:00","id":1180560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180559#post1180559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now that's just mean... \ud83d\ude1c</div> </div> </div> </div>12 more hours...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":".  MIscoalculated the time zone difference. 01-29-2018, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T02:41:05-08:00","id":1180652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180560#post1180560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 12 more hours...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's like 'night before Christmas' jitters, am I right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T04:06:34-08:00","id":1180659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180404#post1180404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Some minor changes to how the Esperanza happened.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHaving written (among other things) the Europe update, I hope people enjoy the changes in presentation and setting we've made for the new edition <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bExcited now that the kickstarter is almost here!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T05:59:22-08:00","id":1180682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180544#post1180544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I would love to be able to pick up a PDF of the Battlegrounds rulebook as a stretch goal or add on.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a related note, the followup book &quot;Trinity: Battleground Players Guide&quot; is <a href=\"https://drivethrurpg.com/product/122127/Trinity-Battleground-Players-Guide\" target=\"_blank\">available for free on DTRPG</a>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T06:41:54-08:00","id":1180690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180682#post1180682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a related note, the followup book &quot;Trinity: Battleground Players Guide&quot; is <a href=\"https://drivethrurpg.com/product/122127/Trinity-Battleground-Players-Guide\" target=\"_blank\">available for free on DTRPG</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T06:53:01-08:00","id":1180694,"title":"","content":"So, this is more a general Onyx Path/White Wolf question, but since two people have identified that they have written for the book, I wanted to ask.<br /> <br /> Usually OP books have a list of writers at the front of the book, but not which sections they worked on. I have always been curious who worked on what, but I'm not sure how to find that out. It's like knowing that you liked one series of books by a particular author, and then seeing their name on something else - I would be curious to read the new thing they did if I liked the last thing they did. However, with the credits system in as it stands I won't know who wrote the FSA section (for example) and I can't follow their work onto other projects.<br /> <br /> Is there a way to get broad strokes of which authors worked on which sections?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T07:12:43-08:00","id":1180697,"title":"","content":"As far as I am aware, the main way that exists is just to ask writers which bits they worked on, as long as you're understanding that not every writer is going to want to or feel comfortable going into such details or, indeed, spending their time on a public internet forum discussing stuff in the first place.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Then there are reprobates such as myself who basically champ at the bit for releases to happen so we can talk to people about stuff we wrote <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T17:02:45-08:00","id":1180936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180530#post1180530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Larssen will be putting up with crap from anyone, including the UN. I guess we'll see what she had to give up to get the veneer of respectability. I wonder what's going to happen to the Second Legion?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Second Legion is now the Sacred Legion. They left the psi order when the UN started tightening the screws and joined the Papal Swiss Guard. Having attained Swiss citizenship through an as-yet-undisclosed deal brokered by everyone's favorite Aesculapian proxy, they serve as the Vatican's psionic Inquisition.<br /> <br /> - C.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Clayton A. Oliver | Formerly Ubiquitous<br /> <br /> <i>When the half-light starts to rise/And the long gone come back again<br /> After the shortcuts and the highs/Comes the pain<br /> And the rain</i>","edited":{"userid":2966,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2966-tegyrius","user":"Tegyrius","date":". 01-30-2018, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2966-tegyrius","name":"Tegyrius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T02:12:59-08:00","id":1181050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180697#post1180697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I am aware, the main way that exists is just to ask writers which bits they worked on, as long as you're understanding that not every writer is going to want to or feel comfortable going into such details or, indeed, spending their time on a public internet forum discussing stuff in the first place.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Then there are reprobates such as myself who basically champ at the bit for releases to happen so we can talk to people about stuff we wrote <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).</div> </div> </div> </div>As Acrozatarim said, the best thing to do is ask. Most of the writers who hang around these forums and post are pretty happy to talk about what they wrote. How else are you going to know which authors you love? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T02:15:57-08:00","id":1181051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tegyrius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180936#post1180936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Second Legion is now the Sacred Legion. They left the psi order when the UN started tightening the screws and joined the Papal Swiss Guard. Having attained Swiss citizenship through an as-yet-undisclosed deal brokered by everyone's favorite Aesculapian proxy, they serve as the Vatican's psionic Inquisition.<br /> <br /> - C.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Laughs* Now I kind of want to write a continuum splinter where this is true. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T03:26:54-08:00","id":1181064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1181050#post1181050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Acrozatarim said, the best thing to do is ask. Most of the writers who hang around these forums and post are pretty happy to talk about what they wrote. How else are you going to know which authors you love? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's always the option of plying us with booze at the Big Bar on 2.<br /> <br /> - C.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Clayton A. Oliver | Formerly Ubiquitous<br /> <br /> <i>When the half-light starts to rise/And the long gone come back again<br /> After the shortcuts and the highs/Comes the pain<br /> And the rain</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2966-tegyrius","name":"Tegyrius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T05:41:40-08:00","id":1181096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1181050#post1181050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Acrozatarim said, the best thing to do is ask. Most of the writers who hang around these forums and post are pretty happy to talk about what they wrote. How else are you going to know which authors you love? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the obvious question is what names are you and Acrozatarim credited as and what sections did you write? =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T10:57:23-08:00","id":1181163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1180697#post1180697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b(Then there are reprobates such as myself who basically champ at the bit for releases to happen so we can talk to people about stuff we wrote <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).</div> </div> </div> </div>While I've never worked on the Trinity Continuum (maybe one day, but not yet), I definitely understand the sentiment. The more I'm seeing of Trinity, the more excited I'm getting. You and all the writers should be very proud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T01:24:10-08:00","id":1181594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1181096#post1181096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the obvious question is what names are you and Acrozatarim credited as and what sections did you write? =D</div> </div> </div> </div>As I\u2019ve already mentioned around these forums, I designed and wrote the new Psi Powers system. As a side to that I wrote a few other systems that AEon needed, mostly because of the Trinity Core/Storypath system didn\u2019t cover a few things that Aptitudes do. A good example was adding in rules for illnesses, because TC didn\u2019t have them (having the flu not being a major part of heroic action stories) but Vitakinesis was severely devalued if it didn\u2019t have a range of things to look at healing.<br /> <br /> I also wrote several of the setting pieces, but please excuse me if I don\u2019t name them before the AEon drafts start being shared, as I want people to go into the material fresh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T09:17:03-08:00","id":1181681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1181594#post1181594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I\u2019ve already mentioned around these forums, I designed and wrote the new Psi Powers system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll understand completely if you don't feel comfortable answering this question in advance of the relevant manuscript dropping <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> How 'baked in' is utilizing momentum and dramatic editing into how the psi powers work? I'm not keen on either of those concepts at all, so I'm eager to find out if I can make use of your Psi powers rules without spending too much time surgically removing those concepts if they're used. Thanks in advance! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T15:29:51-08:00","id":1181824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1181681#post1181681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How 'baked in' is utilizing momentum and dramatic editing into how the psi powers work? I'm not keen on either of those concepts at all, so I'm eager to find out if I can make use of your Psi powers rules without spending too much time surgically removing those concepts if they're used. Thanks in advance! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hard one to answer, as it\u2019s both \u2018not at all\u2019 and \u2018completely\u2019. Let me expand on that a little.<br /> <br /> Dramatic Editing - Psi powers don\u2019t take this into account at all. Psions don\u2019t tend to use dramatic editing, that\u2019s a Talent thing. Individual groups can have psions use DE if they want, since the Storypath system is flexible and designed to allow cross over of the different rules across the Continuum. But the default assumption is that psions don\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Momentum - You might need to give me more on what difficulties you see in using or removing Momentum, because I\u2019m not sure if my next answer hits your concerns. In the sense that you add to the momentum pool when you fail, and take dice from it when you want to use them, the psi system works like every other part of Storypath. Fail a roll, add to the pool. Need a bit of a boost for a dice pool, take from it. I don\u2019t recall that I referenced Momentum at all in the chapter, as it\u2019s just a thing that\u2019s assumed to exist, like Target Numbers. I didn\u2019t reference them either, I just assume people know to roll agains the one that applies to their character. <br /> <br /> So, with that said, if you want to remove momentum from the system, it shouldn\u2019t impact the psi powers as presented at all.<br /> <br /> Does that answer what you\u2019re asking?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T12:25:53-08:00","id":1182041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1181824#post1181824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snipped lots of helpful info</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually really <b>very</b> helpful, yes. Where you said &quot;it\u2019s both \u2018not at all\u2019 and \u2018completely\u2019&quot; - that actually makes perfect sense. If I'm reading that right on momentum, with it being part of the core mechanics then it can come up a lot like the example you gave. But it isn't especially woven into Psi powers specifically from what you're saying, outside the core die roll. That's awesome to hear, I was wondering if there was going to be a bunch of rules saying &quot;and using the momentum pool you can do 'all this extra stuff' with Psi', which would make limiting or removing momentum more challenging. <br /> <br /> I'm not big on group dice pools generally and I avoid meta-currency pools in games for both players and GMs. If I can dodge anything fail-forward related too then I'm good. Those specific mechanics just rub me the wrong way, is all.<br /> <br /> On the DE stuff, OK - that's new info to me about it being more of a Talent thing. That actually makes sense now for Talents, having read the first manuscript. Its nice to see that Psions are going to remain somewhat distinct for those of us <i>only</i> interested in Aeon/Psions.<br /> <br /> I'm <i>very</i> keen to read your take on the Psi powers when the Aeon manuscript drops. I'm especially interested in seeing how the relative power scales all function between the Aptitudes. Not to mentioned how you've incorporated Teleportation (which was arguably not as as low key as the powers in the 1st edition tended to be). <br /> <br /> Thanks for the reply, I really appreciate it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T14:33:40-08:00","id":1182069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1182041#post1182041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it isn't especially woven into Psi powers specifically from what you're saying, outside the core die roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. None of the Psi powers as written have anything that calls for \u2018spend X Momentum to gain Y ability\u2019. (With the caveat that the developer is fully within their rights to change things as they see fit. But to the best of my knowledge, John has seen no reason that the Psi powers need such a mechanism.)<br /> <br /> All Psi powers are run off a dice pool of Psi + Mode. There will be occasions that you\u2019ll want to try and increase your dice pool (or successes) - the psi system is a little more flexible than it was in 1st edition, and you\u2019ll see what I mean in a week or two. For these occasions you\u2019ll improve your chances if you can take advantage of things available under Storypath, such as items or situations that grant Enhancement, for example, or taking a few dice from momentum. But none of these are required to use psi powers.<br /> <br /> I hear what you\u2019re saying about meta-currency, but remember that the Trinity Continuum is a rather narratively-driven universe, where the PCs are heroes who do big things. Talents tap into this most directly with Dramatic Editing to have things go their way, but Psions (and presumably eventually Novas) get some benefit from this with momentum. You can run the game without such things - you might need to do a little tweaking - but the universal assumption (meaning - the universe assumes this to be true) that heroes are heroes and should strive to overcome obstacles, get back up when they\u2019re knocked down, and eventually succeed and reach their goals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1182041#post1182041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm <i>very</i> keen to read your take on the Psi powers when the Aeon manuscript drops. I'm especially interested in seeing how the relative power scales all function between the Aptitudes. Not to mentioned how you've incorporated Teleportation (which was arguably not as as low key as the powers in the 1st edition tended to be).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Aptitudes will be recognisable, but some things are different. Some powers have shifted around, some are gone, some new ones take their place. Some Modes are different, some are pretty consistent with what they were before.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s some cool new stuff in Teleportation, but a lot that will feel familiar to people. <br /> <br /> In terms of power scales, I think I\u2019ve balanced the different Aptitudes pretty well. My overarching design goal was to make players curse that they can only take one Aptitude, and want to play them all. From playtest feedback, I think I\u2019ve hit that goal. <br /> <br /> (I can\u2019t wait to talk more openly about these with all of you!)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1182041#post1182041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the reply, I really appreciate it!</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re welcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 02-03-2018, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T15:29:28-08:00","id":1182093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1182069#post1182069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In terms of power scales, I think I\u2019ve balanced the different Aptitudes pretty well. My overarching design goal was to make players curse that they can only take one Aptitude, and want to play them all. From playtest feedback, I think I\u2019ve hit that goal.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>*shakes fist in Bunyip's direction*<br /> <br /> Curse you, Bunyiiiiip!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T17:00:11-08:00","id":1182117,"title":"","content":"That's a bunch of info, thanks!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1182069#post1182069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct. None of the Psi powers as written have anything that calls for \u2018spend X Momentum to gain Y ability\u2019. (With the caveat that the developer is fully within their rights to change things as they see fit. But to the best of my knowledge, John has seen no reason that the Psi powers need such a mechanism.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood on all points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1182069#post1182069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Psi powers are run off a dice pool of Psi + Mode. There will be occasions that you\u2019ll want to try and increase your dice pool (or successes) - the psi system is a little more flexible than it was in 1st edition, and you\u2019ll see what I mean in a week or two. For these occasions you\u2019ll improve your chances if you can take advantage of things available under Storypath, such as items or situations that grant Enhancement, for example, or taking a few dice from momentum. But none of these are required to use psi powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, so there's some flexibility through the powers themselves and, say, Enhancements, if I pull momentum. Now its just waiting to read the specifics <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1182069#post1182069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....but the universal assumption (meaning - the universe assumes this to be true) that heroes are heroes and should strive to overcome obstacles, get back up when they\u2019re knocked down, and eventually succeed and reach their goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, understood and that makes sense if that's what you're looking for in a game. I do find &quot;heroes are heroes who eventually succeed&quot; frankly a little boring and and something of a cliche, personally. I especially dislike mechanics that <i>proscribe</i> that stuff. I <i>do</i> love seeing shades of grey in protagonists and eventual success not being a given however (even more as a player than GM); which was one of the many things that drew me to Aeon in the first place. It helps that I'm not interested in the wider Continuum of games either, I'm just here for Aeon. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1182069#post1182069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Aptitudes will be recognisable, but some things are different. Some powers have shifted around, some are gone, some new ones take their place. Some Modes are different, some are pretty consistent with what they were before. There\u2019s some cool new stuff in Teleportation, but a lot that will feel familiar to people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, now that's all <i>very</i> interesting. Damnit, couldn't we have started with the Aeon manuscript previews? :-P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1182069#post1182069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of power scales, I think I\u2019ve balanced the different Aptitudes pretty well. My overarching design goal was to make players curse that they can only take one Aptitude, and want to play them all. From playtest feedback, I think I\u2019ve hit that goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was one of the issues I had with the 1st ed powers - players tended to find they each really only wanted to play one or two Aptitudes (sometimes influenced by being tied to specific order allegiances). With order membership being a bit more fluid this time, plus what you've said here, I'm really curious to see how players react to this stuff now. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1182069#post1182069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I can\u2019t wait to talk more openly about these with all of you!)</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure! Thanks for the followup. Fascinating stuff indeed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T19:13:22-08:00","id":1182149,"title":"","content":"For those who don\u2019t hang out on other forums, I\u2019m just going to cut and paste some tid-bits about Psi powers that John Snead is dropping over on rpg.net. There are some info-drops on new stuff in there... <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throwing gouts of fire or cryogenic cold is a 2 dot thermokinesis ability, it starts off being about as good as an assault rifle, and goes up to being as good as an anti-tank weapon. 3 dots gets you the ability to armor yourself in fire or ice, 4 &amp; 5 dots of thermokinesis are even more powerful. Flight is a 3 dot TK power (as is being your own TK rifle). Flying at supersonic speed in a car, while carrying other people and cars along with you is 4 dots in TK. Then there's Perikinesis, the force field Mode of PK...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much everyone has an augmented reality cellphone, and Network is now a 1 dot Mindshare ability that costs 0 psi points to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T22:09:19-08:00","id":1182179,"title":"","content":"Will Psiads in other settings have different mechanics on some of the Modes, since there's a different power balance resulting from what everyone else can do with easily accessible tech?<br /> <br /> Or I suppose, that's what the weaker Psychomorphs in Adventure! (along with Exomorphs and Paramorphs) will be for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T01:40:02-08:00","id":1182199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1182179#post1182179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will Psiads in other settings have different mechanics on some of the Modes, since there's a different power balance resulting from what everyone else can do with easily accessible tech?<br /> <br /> Or I suppose, that's what the weaker Psychomorphs in Adventure! (along with Exomorphs and Paramorphs) will be for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Impossible to answer that, I\u2019m afraid. You\u2019re asking how mechanics are going to work for settings/things that haven\u2019t been written yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T01:51:14-08:00","id":1182201,"title":"","content":"Fair enough","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T03:20:22-08:00","id":1182211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1182069#post1182069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My overarching design goal was to make players curse that they can only take one Aptitude, and want to play them all. From playtest feedback, I think I\u2019ve hit that goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't remember if I specifically acknowledged this in my own playtest reports, but Auxiliary Modes were pretty popular with my players for basically this reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T09:08:21-08:00","id":1182283,"title":"","content":"I like everything I'm reading regarding aptitudes in this thread. Thanks for asking the question and thanks for the informative replies. This information, along with replies in another thread, has convinced me to go ahead an back this while the backing is good.<br /> <br /> Chill, I can relate to your take on momentum-like mechanics. I'm encouraged to see it sounds pretty modular in that it seems pretty straightforward to just ignore that mechanic and still play the rest of the game. For my part, if I end up running this, I'm sure my <i>players</i> would enjoy the option and it would only have the potential on frustrating my occasional GM sadism if the team cakewalks every potential butt-whupping the NPCs can muster. So I'll probably try it to start. and see how it goes.<br /> <br /> MythicFox, some of my players tried Auxiliary Modes also. I liked how the option for auxiliaries were a meta-hint (well, a baked-in setting hint, too, I suppose) that there was some ulterior motives behind the Doyen's Promethean &quot;Gift&quot;. Will there be the option for auxiliaries in this new edition? I have no strong feelings either way, just curious. One of my favorite things about the setting is limiting the players to one core aptitude. I love how it almost necessitates teamwork to pull off great successes. I also approve of it preventing the Silar-like (from Heroes) characters whose power is I-Have-All-The-Powers. Unless that person is an aberrant necessitating the unity of our heroes to defend against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23804-uri-meca","name":"Uri Meca","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T15:14:30-08:00","id":1182405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uri Meca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1182283#post1182283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be the option for auxiliaries in this new edition? I have no strong feelings either way, just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Auxiliary Modes are substantially the same as in 1st ed. You can purchase the first dot in a Mode from another Aptitude. You can purchase multiple first dots from multiple Modes from multiple Aptitudes if you want. <br /> <br /> Auxiliary Modes are a little more versatile than they were before. Every Aptitude has a couple of basic \u20180-dot powers\u2019 that everyone with even one dot in any Mode from the Aptitude gets. None of them are earth-shattering, but they\u2019re certainly useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T07:13:57-08:00","id":1182588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1179503-trinity-developers-on-16miles2hell?p=1181096#post1181096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the obvious question is what names are you and Acrozatarim credited as and what sections did you write? =D</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think my name's in my sig <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bSections-wise, my contributions are pretty wide-ranging - some setting material, some of the chargen section, most of the new Paths, some of the Aeon-specific extra rules, some sample NPCs. I'll stick with Leath's lead and not specify which bit of setting material was mine until the preview's out and people have had some time to digest it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}